//     directory so that test-time writes (vitest's .vite-temp, etc.) stay
//     inside the sandboxed cwd instead of following a symlink OUT to the
//     source (which nono --allow-cwd refuses → EPERM).
//   • Each child is evaluated RECURSIVELY: small dirs/files are COPIED
//     (real, writable, isolated), large dirs/files (>= threshold) are
//     SYMLINKED to share read-mostly payload, and symlink entries are
//     recreated as link nodes.
//   • Recursion is bounded: max depth 16, byte budget per top-level entry
//     (thresholdBytes). On overflow the subtree is symlinked and a
//     verify_overlay_skipped warn event is emitted.
